course: dictionary
lesson: 4151
title: Science words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Science books use special words, and you can work many of them out from the words around them. Read the whole sentence first, then ask what word would fit. «Large studies found MSG (a powder added to food to make it taste savoury) safe for most people in normal amounts.» The brackets explain MSG, and that helps you understand what the sentence is about.
explain: Now look at «tomatoes and cheese have natural glutamate too». The word natural is a clue: glutamate is already in these foods, not added by a factory. The word too also tells you that glutamate is in something else in the sentence, so it is found in food that people already eat.
explain: Some words in a sentence give you a clue about the taste or the feeling. The word savoury appears in the sentence, and it tells you that glutamate is linked to a rich, meaty or cheesy taste, not a sweet one. When you see a word you don't know, check the clues first, then use a dictionary to confirm.
fact: Glutamate is a natural substance found in many foods, such as tomatoes, cheese and mushrooms.
fact: Glutamate gives the savoury taste called umami, which is one of the five tastes: sweet, sour, salty, bitter and umami.
fact: Monosodium glutamate (MSG) is a salt of glutamate, added to food to make it taste more savoury.
fact: In the brain, nerve cells use glutamate as a chemical messenger to pass signals.
fact: Some food labels list MSG as a flavour enhancer, which means it makes the flavour stronger.
exercise: «Tomatoes and cheese have natural glutamate too.» Where does the glutamate in this sentence come from? | A factory that makes salt | A kitchen spice rack | *Foods that are already natural, such as tomatoes and cheese | The brain's nerve cells only
exercise: Glutamate gives the savoury taste called umami. Which of the five tastes is umami? | *Savoury | Sweet | Bitter | Sour
exercise: Monosodium glutamate is written as MSG on a food label. What does it do to food? | It makes the food cold | It removes the salt | It makes the food sweeter | *It makes the food taste more savoury
test: What is glutamate? | *A natural substance found in foods such as mushrooms | A type of metal used in batteries | A colour used to paint food | A sweet fruit from the tropics
test: In the sentence «Large studies found MSG safe for most people in normal amounts», what does the word safe mean? | Very salty | Full of flavour | *Not harmful | Lost or missing
exam: Which sentence uses the word glutamate correctly? | Glutamate is the name of a school subject. | Glutamate is a sweet fruit grown on trees. | We use glutamate to paint the walls. | *Mushrooms and tomatoes contain natural glutamate, which gives food a savoury taste.
